=== SIGNATURE ===
z_opt(default, [val], [keep_text])

=== COMMENT ===
Helper for optional single-value arguments: returns default when val is omitted, a blank cell, or ""; otherwise val collapsed to a true scalar (z_scalar), with a number stored as text converted to a number unless keep_text is TRUE. Use as mode, z_opt(0, match_mode) in place of IF(ISOMITTED(...)).

=== CODE ===
=LAMBDA(default, [val], [keep_text],
  IF(ISOMITTED(val), default,
    LET(v, z_scalar(val),
      IF(OR(ISBLANK(val)), default,
      IF(AND(ISTEXT(v), v = ""), default,
      IF(OR(IF(ISOMITTED(keep_text), FALSE, keep_text), NOT(ISTEXT(v))), v,
         IFERROR(VALUE(v), v))))))
)

=== DESCRIPTION ===
Private helper that gives every optional single-value argument the same, forgiving behaviour. Call it where a lambda used to write IF(ISOMITTED(x), default, x):

  mode, z_opt(0, match_mode)
  sep,  z_opt(";", delim, TRUE)

Rules, in order:
  1. argument omitted                     -> default
  2. a blank cell (or an all-blank range)  -> default   (pointing an unused argument at an empty cell is the same as leaving it out)
  3. empty text ""                         -> default   (e.g. a config cell whose formula returned "")
  4. otherwise the value, collapsed to a true scalar by z_scalar (so TOCOL(x) / {x} behave like x), and
  5. a number stored as text ("2", "-1") is converted to the number - unless keep_text is TRUE, which delimiters and other genuinely-text options should pass so that "0" or "1" stay text.

Because an omitted parameter stays omitted when it is passed on to another lambda, z_opt can test ISOMITTED on the caller's behalf. Arrays bigger than 1x1 pass through rules 4-5 unchanged (a blank range still hits rule 2), so it is safe on arguments that may legitimately be arrays, such as xfilter's masks.

Do not use it on an argument that must stay a range reference (a board or boundary whose position matters) - z_scalar reads the cell's value and the reference is lost - nor on a value that is looked up in data, where "2" and 2 must stay distinct.

Arguments:
  default     - the value to use when val is omitted, blank or "".
  [val]       - the caller's optional argument, passed straight through.
  [keep_text] - TRUE to leave numeric text as text (default FALSE).

Returns:
  default, or val normalised as above.

Example:
  z_opt(1, )            ->  1
  z_opt(1, A1)          ->  1 when A1 is empty, otherwise A1's value
  z_opt(0, "2")         ->  2
  z_opt(";", "0", TRUE) ->  "0"
